(CLI-06: `--lib-path <paths>` - additional library search paths
 (comma-separated). Unlike --link (CLI-05/Discrepancy 1), this one is
 load-bearing: when the .lib/.so pair lives outside the source's own
 directory, compilation fails without it and succeeds with it. NOT
 runnable as a single file by check-probes.sh's fixed invocation: needs
 a prebuilt libtally.so/.lib pair (CLI-04) in a SUBDIRECTORY relative to
 this source.
 RE-VERIFIED 2026-08-22 against vox 0.4.9: transcript below re-runs
 byte-for-byte identical (using CLI-04.vox's now-fixed, --shared-clean
 source to build libtally.so -- see that file's header).
 Transcript (lib in ./libs, source beside ./libs, not inside it):
   $ vox tally_lib.vox --shared -o libs/libtally.so
   $ vox tally_user.vox -o u1                    (no --lib-path)
   Error: could not find the library interface file './libtally.lib'.
   Paths tried:
     libtally.lib
   Use --lib-path <dir> to add directories to this search.
   $ vox tally_user.vox -o u2 --lib-path ./libs  (with --lib-path)
   $ ./u2
   42
 Ran: (not runnable as a single file; see transcript above)
)
see tally version "1.0" from "./libtally.lib".

